{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Resolve Freight Reference"},"description":"Resolve an arbitrary freight identifier \u2014 one opaque string in, typed and cited candidates out. Use when you hold one identifier-ish token (\"176\", \"UN1845\", \"NLRTM\", \"FOB\", \"22G1\", \"MSKU1100810\", \"D/E\", \"TU9\") and do not know what kind of identifier it is: each candidate names its entity type and carries the api_url and canonical_url of its full record. q is ONE identifier (max 32 chars), or an fu: identifier (fu_id or fu_version_id, up to 200 chars), which resolves to exactly its one record or to none. Colliding grammars return several ranked candidates, never a silent guess; zero candidates is a valid result. Single-token resolution, not free-text extraction \u2014 pass one identifier, not a manifest line. The lookups it resolves into: adr_lookup, airline_lookup, airport_lookup, unlocode_lookup, hs_code_lookup, incoterms_lookup, container_lookup, uld_lookup, validate. Rate-limited: a limit error carries reset_at, the UTC time the allowance resets.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"q":{"description":"One freight identifier, or an fu: identifier from an answer (e.g. \"fu:adr:un:1203:II:F1@2025\").","maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["q"],"type":"object"},"name":"resolve_reference","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":true,"properties":{"_source":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"authority_current_edition":{"type":"string"},"checked":{"type":"string"},"checked_at":{"type":"string"},"dataset_edition":{"type":"string"},"name":{"type":"string"},"provenance_status":{"enum":["verified","pending-verification","computed","live"],"type":"string"},"source_url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name",